# Normalize every tracked text file to LF.
#
# This repository is edited on Windows. With core.autocrlf=false a CRLF working
# tree is compared byte-for-byte against an LF index, so every file that a
# Windows editor touched showed up as a large false "modification". Declaring
# `text eol=lf` makes git apply the CRLF->LF clean filter on comparison, which
# keeps Windows checkouts noise-free while never committing CRLF into the repo.
#
# Only text formats are listed. A `text` attribute on a binary file would corrupt
# it, so binaries keep the default (auto-detected) behaviour.

*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.md            text eol=lf
*.sql           text eol=lf
*.php           text eol=lf
*.json          text eol=lf
.gitignore      text eol=lf
.gitattributes  text eol=lf
